  "commit_message": "fix(kudos): heart button now disables in-flight and for anonymous own kudos\n\n`kudos_cards` gains a server-computed `is_own` column (migration 0016) so\nthe sender of an ANONYMOUS kudo can be told apart from everyone else even\nthough `sender_id` is masked NULL for them (0009) — the heart button no\nlonger renders enabled only to have RLS silently reject the toggle\n(F008 BR-005). `useKudosHearts` also now exposes `pendingIds` as\nrender-visible state, folded into `heartDisabled`, so a toggle disables\nits own button until the server answers (BR-004). Un-fixmes `[C26]`\n(now exercised via a real self-sent kudo) and adds `[C34]` for the\nanonymous case; kudos.ts/kudos-client.tsx split to stay under the\n200-line convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
